/// Germany, as far as a US citizen living there needs it.
///
/// German income tax and social contributions are taken from pay by the employer,
/// and the bank withholds a flat tax on interest, so what matters here is
/// counting them: they are foreign taxes paid, in dollars, which a return can
/// credit (Form 1116) or ignore when the pay is excluded (Form 2555).
///
/// SAMPLE DATA. Nothing here is checked against the Bundeszentralamt fuer
/// Steuern; German rates are not modelled because the employer withholds.
system us/abroad/de

use us/abroad


/// The German tax authorities.
entity finanzamt : government

/// German tax withheld from pay or from interest. What arrives counts as foreign
/// tax already paid.
kind de-tax : expense

/// Tax paid to Germany, counted in dollars at the rate of the day.
law count-de-tax
  on in
  when to is de-tax
  count value(amount, USD) as foreign-tax-paid
